    lembaga_note_table:'A party takes part in seat allocation if its vote share in this table reaches the threshold you enter. This suits cases where all the votes that decide the threshold are in the table, such as a national result or trying a different threshold size.',
    lembaga_note_manual:'Each party\'s eligibility is set with the <strong>Passed threshold</strong> checkbox rather than computed from the votes in the table. Use this when the threshold is computed from votes outside the district being calculated. An example is the 2024 DPR RI election, which used a 4% threshold of national valid votes (Law 7/2017 Article 414(1)), so a party strong in one district still won no seat there if it failed nationally. Unchecked parties keep their votes on record but take no part in seat allocation.',
    lembaga_note_none:'Every party takes part in seat allocation with no vote-share requirement. In the 2024 election this applied to provincial and regency/city DPRD (Law 7/2017 Article 414(2)). It can also simulate a DPR election with no parliamentary threshold, which became relevant after Constitutional Court Decision No. 116/PUU-XXI/2023 ordered the 4% threshold to be revised before the 2029 election.',
